  "worked_solution": "Here, we apply the quotient rule and the power rule to get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{z\\to (-4)}\\frac{{({z}^{2}-10)}^{2}}{(z+6)^{5}} & =\\frac{{lim}_{z\\to (-4)}{({z}^{2}-10)}^{2}}{{lim}_{z\\to (-4)}(z+6)^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{({lim}_{z\\to (-4)}({z}^{2}-10))}^{2}}{{({lim}_{z\\to (-4)}(z+6))}^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{((-4)^{2}-10)}^{2}}{(-4+6)^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}}{{2}^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
